at he  signed  and now that it suits him he's trying to  bring it down again there is a great  deal of cynicism here but there is  already reaction from mauro sefkovic the  eu's chief negotiator talking about this  uh saying that the northern ireland  protocol is the only method that you by  which you can balance the requirements  of the good friday agreement and the  requirements of the eu's single market i  think we can listen now to just a little  bit of mr sefekovich talking also about  in his mind the impossibility of  renegotiating the protocol  renegotiating of the protocol is  unrealistic  no workable alternative solution has  been found to this delicate  long-negotiated  balance any renegotiations would simply  bring further legal uncertainty for the  people and businesses in northern  ireland  for these reasons the european union  will not renegotiate the protocol  this position uh we're in this curious  position whereby both sides are in  effect making the same argument in the  uk and uh across the eu basis saying  they are the ones protecting the good  friday agreement both sides insisting  that they are open uh to negotiation and  it is the others who are being dogmatic  of course one profound difference is the  eu says you cannot bring down this  protocol the uk is saying it you need to  and one other thing is i said to you a  little earlier that i thought it was  very likely that the legal proceedings  would start soon against the uk  i think that is ever more likely i think  that process will begin in the next 48  hours or so three things may happen one  is that a former process that was frozen  will be unfrozen secondly  more proceedings will be started that is  in the terms of the trade agreement and  thirdly by the way there is this  prospect uh that if this becomes ever  more rancorous that there could be  tariff  in the start of a trade war and and  there is a thought that terrorists could  be introduced on industries who are  based in the constituencies of  high-profile mps problem is i'm told  that they've looked at places like  uxbridge and norfolk and not found many  industries that actually  could be heard  by eu terrace but that is the level of  negotiation we've got to make no mistake  this is turning into a very very bitter  argument yeah absolutely adam thanks  very much adam parsons there in  brussels stephen murphy and rob powell  thank you all

